A minimal four-orbital Bloch Hamiltonian H(\mathbf{k}) = s_{0}H_{0}(\mathbf{k}) + H_{\mathrm{SOC}}(\mathbf{k}) was constructed where H_{0}(\mathbf{k}) is the spinless part given explicitly by
      $$
      \begin{aligned}
      H_{0} &= \Big[\tfrac{\mu_{p}}{2}+t_{px}\cos(a k_{x})+t_{py}\cos(b k_{y})\Big]\Gamma_{1}^{-}
      +\Big[\tfrac{\mu_{d}}{2}+t_{dx}\cos(a k_{x})\Big]\Gamma_{1}^{+} \\
      &\quad + t_{dAB}e^{-i b k_{y}}\big(1+e^{i a k_{x}}\big)e^{i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{1}}\Gamma_{2}^{+}
      +t_{pAB}\big(1+e^{i a k_{x}}\big)e^{i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{2}}\Gamma_{2}^{-}\\
      &\quad + t_{0AB}\big(1-e^{i a k_{x}}\big)e^{i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{3}}\Gamma_{3}
      -2i t_{0x}\sin(a k_{x})\big[e^{i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{4}}\Gamma_{4}^{+}+e^{-i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{4}}\Gamma_{4}^{-}\big]
      +\mathrm{H.c.},
      \end{aligned}
      $$
      and the SOC part H_{\mathrm{SOC}}(\mathbf{k}) is given explicitly as
      $$
      \begin{aligned}
      H_{\mathrm{SOC}}&=\Big[(\lambda_{dx}^{z}s_{z}+\lambda_{dx}^{y}s_{y})\sin(ak_{x})\Big]\Gamma_{5}^{+}
      +\Big[(\lambda_{px}^{z}s_{z}+\lambda_{px}^{y}s_{y})\sin(ak_{x})\Big]\Gamma_{5}^{-}\\
      &\quad -i\lambda_{AB}^{y}s_{y}\big(1+e^{iak_{x}}\big)e^{i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{3}}\Gamma_{6}
      -i\big(\lambda_{0}^{z}s_{z}+\lambda_{0}^{y}s_{y}\big)\Big(e^{i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{4}}\Gamma_{4}^{+}-e^{-i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{4}}\Gamma_{4}^{-}\Big)\\
      &\quad -i\big(\lambda_{0}^{'z}s_{z}+\lambda_{0}^{'y}s_{y}\big)\Big(e^{-i b k_{y}}e^{i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{4}}\Gamma_{4}^{+}-e^{i b k_{y}}e^{-i\mathbf{k}\cdot\Delta_{4}}\Gamma_{4}^{-}\Big)
      +\mathrm{H.c.},
      \end{aligned}
      $$
      with Pauli spin matrices s_{x,y,z}. The orbital-space matrices Γ_i are defined as linear combinations of products of Pauli matrices τ_j (acting on the sublattice degree of freedom) and σ_i (acting on the orbital degree of freedom): Γ_0 = τ_0 σ_0, Γ_1^± = τ_0 (σ_0 ± σ_3)/2, Γ_2^± = (τ_1 + i τ_2)(σ_0 ± σ_3)/4, Γ_3 = (τ_1 + i τ_2) i σ_2/2, Γ_4^± = (τ_0 ± τ_3)(σ_1 + i σ_2)/4, Γ_5^± = τ_3 (σ_0 ± σ_3)/2, Γ_6 = (τ_1 + i τ_2) σ_1/2. The vectors Δ_i are defined as differences between lattice site positions: Δ_1 = r_Ad - r_Bd, Δ_2 = r_Ap - r_Bp, Δ_3 = r_Ad - r_Bp, Δ_4 = r_Ad - r_Ap, with the site coordinates r_Ad = (-0.25a, 0.32b), r_Bp = (0.25a, 0.07b), r_Ap = (-0.25a, -0.07b), r_Bd = (0.25a, -0.32b), and lattice constants a = 3.477 Å, b = 6.249 Å. The numerical values of the Hamiltonian parameters are: μ_p = -1.75 eV, μ_d = 0.74 eV, t_px = 1.13 eV, t_dx = -0.41 eV, t_pAB = 0.40 eV, t_dAB = 0.51 eV, t_0AB = 0.39 eV, t_0ABx = 0.29 eV, t_0x = 0.14 eV, t_py = 0.13 eV; SOC parameters: λ_dx^z = -0.008 eV, λ_dx^y = -0.031 eV, λ_px^z = -0.010 eV, λ_px^y = -0.040 eV, λ_AB^y = 0.011 eV, λ_0^z = 0.012 eV, λ_0^y = 0.051 eV, λ_0'^z = 0.012 eV, λ_0'^y = 0.050 eV.
